00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:57.500
A volume confirmation filter requires that any momentum or catalyst trade must print volume

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:03.060
at least 50% above its 20-day average on the entry day before capital is committed.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:09.640
Today's mixed global session shows why this matters. AI stocks rebounded on Wall Street,

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:15.240
but Korean shares slumped on lighter volume, illustrating how headline-driven moves without

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:21.000
participation often fade. Implementation is straightforward on any brokerage platform.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:27.100
Pull the 20-day average volume line on a daily chart and compare it to the current bar before

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:35.020
entering. This approach worked best during the 2023-2024 semiconductor rotation when volume spikes

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:41.300
preceded sustained sector outperformance. The risk is missing fast gaps that later proved durable.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:46.560
The same filter would have kept the portfolio out of several low volume defense-related

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:52.400
bounces reported this week. That discipline connects directly to the deeper mechanics of how volume

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:59.820
validates technical levels. Imagine you bought an energy ETF last week after an Iraq output headline

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:05.840
pushed crude higher. Your order filled at the ask during the first 30 minutes when volume was still

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:12.040
thin. The mechanism that actually moved price was the 50-day moving average acting as dynamic

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:20.680
resistance while RSI-14 climbed from 48-62 on expanding volume. Yet the 200-day average remained

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:28.140
4% above, capping upside until a close above both averages occurs. What most retail investors miss

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:34.660
is that a golden cross only carries statistical edge when accompanied by volume at least 30% above

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:41.420
average. Without it, the pattern often fails within two weeks. Professionals always check the MACD

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:47.920
histogram slope before the cross itself. Because a flattening histogram signals fading momentum even

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:53.660
if the lines are about to cross. The biggest mistake with technical analysis is treating every support

00:03:53.660 --> 00:04:00.360
or resistance level as equally valid. Instead, always weight levels by the volume traded at that price

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:06.540
in the prior 20 sessions. Technical rules like these set the stage for today's decision to stay on

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:13.260
